                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">British Proposal Made at Meeting of Six
                        Delegations May 25 But Not Accepted by Other Delegations</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">supervision</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">A. <hi rendition="#italic">General Principles</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Commissions shall be set up in each of the three States.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>These shall be composed of representatives of neutral countries not
                        members of the present Conference to be chosen by agreement at the
                        Conference.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In Vietnam mixed groups consisting of representatives of the two Commands
                        shall also be set up to function under the authority of the Neutral
                        Commission.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">B. <hi rendition="#italic">Immediate Action</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Representatives of the two Commands, meeting in Geneva, to prepare plans
                        for the constitution and operation of the proposed mixed groups in
                        Vietnam.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Conference to examine the constitution and membership of the proposed
                        Neutral Commissions.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
